# Workflow Requirements

- Write "Following your guidelines!" at the start of messages when you've read the corresponding rule file
- Always ask clarifying questions before implementing
- Show plan/approach first, implement only after approval
- Explain implementations in detail but in simple terms
- Check for existing components that can be reused before creating new ones
- Follow existing file's programming style for consistency
- Keep files small — move reusable functions to utils folder
- Use services folder for backend logic, custom hooks or service files for frontend
- Create reusable components and place in appropriate folders

# Critical Thinking & Code Integrity

- Always question and evaluate user proposals — never mindlessly agree just to appease
- Only follow user's approach if it's truly the best solution; otherwise propose improvements
- Stand firm on optimizations and improved readability when they are genuinely better
- Don't revert good changes just because user asks for explanations — explain why the change is better
- Never touch or modify code unrelated to the current task
- Challenge ideas respectfully and provide alternative solutions when appropriate
- For bugs: reflect on 5-7 possible sources, distill to 1-2 most likely, add logs to validate assumptions before implementing a fix

# Core Principles

- Code should look like it was written by the same developer — follow project patterns
- Clean, readable code over performance optimization
- Never over-engineer; keep it simple
- DRY principles and separation of concerns
- Early returns for readability
- Never guess or assume — always ask clarifying questions
- Never delete existing comments or whitespace between functions

# MCP Integration

- Always use context7 MCP server for official documentation when available
- Use available MCP tools for shadcn via cursor plugin
- Repeat until all relevant docs are fetched for the question
